These relationships are '''optional enrichments, not forced migrations'''. Independently meaningful general-science articles can be retained alongside method pages. Verify terminology, factual claims, scope, duplicate identities and links before new articles or redirects.

== Editorial workflow and stewardship ==

* Write the page that accurately explains the actual subject; use [[BITwiki:Page format]] as flexible grammar, not a mandatory template.
* Source major claims and preserve distinctions among observation, inference, theory, mathematical model, philosophical interpretation and speculation.
* Use semantic relations when justified; do not fabricate a generic computational edge as admission theater.
* Preserve coherent Simple/Core/Technical presentations and historical lineages. Missing reading depths are quality opportunities, not automatic exclusion.
* Renames, merges, redirects, deletions, major ontology edits and live deployments require separate review and dependency assessment. This policy itself changes none of them.
* Reconsider claims and coverage when evidence changes. This page records the corrected admission decision; outstanding quality work belongs in the current editorial workflow.

== Policy correction and history ==

The 2026-11-16 computational-only admission test, including proposed context-only treatment of valid scientific topics for lacking an independently demonstrated computational function, is '''superseded'''. It was an overly narrow editorial interpretation, '''not a scope restriction established by the project owner'''. The repo and archived source histories preserve earlier text for audit. This correction does not certify any claim as scientifically true, rewrite archived V1 writing, or publish to live MediaWiki.

